cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "RSS-based Localization using Distributed Spectrum Sensing for 5G Networks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dhariwal"
    given-names: "Aakarsh"
    affiliation: "Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg (FAU)"
abstract: >-
  Master's thesis evaluating RSS-based active-transmitter localization (MSE
  and LIvE methods) and radio environment map (REM) construction from a
  distributed spectrum-sensing network, extended to a 5G-NR-style OFDM
  transmit waveform and spatially correlated shadowing. Chair of Electrical
  Smart City Systems, FAU Erlangen-Nürnberg, supervised by Victor Shatov and
  Prof. Dr.-Ing. Norman Franchi.
date-released: "2023-10-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aakarshdhariwal/rss-localization-5g-spectrum-sensing"
keywords:
  - received signal strength
  - transmitter localization
  - radio environment map
  - distributed spectrum sensing
  - 5G
  - OFDM
  - shadowing correlation
  - wireless sensor networks
